			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Anthem is a growing European based raid guild. We are always on the lookout for more competent players to fill our ranks and strengthen the guild. Joining Anthem means you will be expected to raid. Not every hour of everyday, but we do raid often. We raid/play from 7 pm CET - 12 pm CET on weekdays, and 1pm CET - 2 am CET on weekends.
<br />

<br />

<br />
Anthem is not a public raid guild, and we do not support raiding with the public. We do not allow any raids outside the guild during our prime time, which runs from 19:00 to 24:00 CET. Additionally, we keep a short list of targets that you under no circumstances may aid anyone but the guild in killing. Breaking this rule can result in termination of your Pm time.
<br />

<br />

<br />
Anthems High Priority currently is*:
<br />
PoW
<br />
PoE / PoEb 
<br />
PoF
<br />
PoA
<br />
Vex Thal.
<br />
Rallon Zek 
<br />

<br />
*Anthems HP targets changes continously
<br />

<br />
If you cannot live with those terms, Anthem is probably not the guild for you.
<br />

<br />
Next, to get the  tag over your head there are some requirements to meet.
<br />

<br />
First off, you must apply to become a PM. In order to become a PM, there are several criterias that much be fullfilled:
<br />

<br />
1. You must be able to raid during our hours.
<br />
2. You must have a sponsor who has been a member for more         than 1 month.
<br />
3. You must fullfill the level / AA / flag requirements
<br />
5. You must have one right click item, indoor usuable.
<br />
6. PM'ing without a sponsor can be a possiblity after a one week evaluation by the officers.
<br />
7. You must have a raidattendance of 50% to become guilded.
<br />

<br />

<br />
Level requirement is 65 for all classes.
<br />
Different classes has different requirements to meet to be able to PM to Anthem. 
<br />

<br />
Although High raid attendence can make up for less AA and flags, at the recruitment-officers evaluation.
<br />

<br />
Low Demand: ShadowKnight Necromancer
<br />

<br />

<br />
Normal Demand: Warrior Shaman Druid Enchanter
<br />

<br />
High Demand: Cleric Monk Bard Wizard Rogue Ranger Berzerker Mage Beastlord Paladin
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
AA's --------------Flags----------- 
<br />

<br />
LD = 200aa's * LP on bert or LMM to Sol Ro tower flagged 
<br />
ND = 75 aa's * MB, grummus, PoNb, TT, PoJ , Caprin 
<br />
HD = 40 aa's * MB, grummus, PoNb, TT, PoJ , Caprin 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Tank minimum HP
<br />

<br />
Paladin &amp; Shadowknight : 4800 unbuffed
<br />
Warrior : 6300 unbuffed
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
MUST have AA/ Spells
<br />
Bard: Instrument Mastery 3
<br />
Beastlord: MGB, Pet hold
<br />
Cleric: MGB 
<br />
Druid: MGB, pure blood
<br />
Enchanter: MGB
<br />
Mage: Pet hold 
<br />
Monk: Rapid Feign 3
<br />
Necromancer: Pet hold, call to corpse
<br />
Paladin: Combat Agility 3
<br />
Rangers: Archery 3
<br />
Rogues: SoS
<br />
Shadowknight: Combat Agility 3
<br />
Shamans: MGB, Blood of Nadox 
<br />
Warriors: AE taunt, Combat Agility 3
<br />
Wizards: Spell Casting Fury 3
<br />

<br />
AA guide 
<br />

<br />
These AA is the ones we find most important for your class to have. 
<br />

<br />
Warriors = CA3, CS3, LR5, AE taunt
<br />
Bards = FM, EN3, IM3, SM3,
<br />
Clerics = MBG, HG3,HA3, MC,SCM 
<br />
Enchanters = MBG, MC3,GM, eldritch rune 
<br />
Necros = Pet hold, ND3, CM3, CtC,
<br />
Paladins = CS3,CA3,LR5,ND3
<br />
Shadowknights = CS3,CA3,LR5,IHT,
<br />
Rangers = EQ, AM3, ND3, CF3, 
<br />
Rogues = SoS, escape, CF3, Ambiexterity
<br />
Monks = rf3,ca3,Nd3,lr5
<br />
Shamans = MBG, canni5, ND3, SCRM
<br />
Druids = MBG, HA3, HG3, Sotw3
<br />
Wizards = SCF3, SCS3, IF,AF, HoD
<br />
Magicians = SCS3, scm3, pet hold, fury3
<br />
Beastlords = MGB, Paragon, ND3, Pet hold
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
If you fullfill the list above, make a post and tell us about yourself, tell us why you want to join Anthem (very important), who your sponsor is (remember, he/she must have agreed to this), if you got a magelo profile a link to it is welcomed.
<br />

<br />
Before you are officaly accepted as a PM for anthem the following steps have to be taken:
<br />

<br />
1. Application posted, with a sponsor included.
<br />
2. Post required from your sponsor presenting the prospect to members.
<br />
3. Initial screening, a few days of feedback from members untill access to our PM-channel is handed out.
<br />
4. After around 2-3 weeks you will be guilded on trial. This is to make it easier for us to get to know you.
<br />
5. After a guilded trial time of 2 weeks, you will be put up for vote.
<br />

<br />
To become trial guilded, you must have a raidattendance of 50% or more!
<br />

<br />
If you do not have Vex Thal key, those raids will not be counted in your raidattendance.
<br />

<br />
When your PM time is done, Anthems members vote if they think you are the material for Anthem.
<br />

<br />
You will need the following:
<br />

<br />
* 90 % PM becomes member.
<br />
* 85% - 90% Officers decide whether to guild the PM right away or extend the PM time. 
<br />
* 80% - 85 % PM is offered extended PM time.
<br />
* Below 80% You are not accepted as member. 
<br />

<br />
Important:
<br />

<br />
Note that our guild raid rules will most likely prevent you from getting any loot on the raid while you are not a full member. Do not expect any. However, you will of course be reimbursed for any reagent costs. 
<br />

<br />
Should loot be rotting, PM's might be allowed to loot it. PM loot is handled on an award basis, at the descretion of the officers of Anthem.  Zhildania Na'Viir
<br />
Enchanting Officer Of Anthem
<br />
My Zhilly Stuff
<br />
